# Environment for `cloud/functions`, copy to `.env` BEFORE the first
# `firebase deploy --only functions`.
#
# ⛔ NOT `.env.aglyn-main`, which is what this file used to say. `.firebaserc`
# maps the alias `aglyn-main` to the project id `aglyn-main`, so that filename
# is BOTH the projectId dotenv and the projectAlias dotenv and firebase-tools
# refuses the deploy outright:
#
#   Error: Can't have both dotenv files with projectId (env.aglyn-main)
#   and projectAlias (.env.aglyn-main) as extensions.
#
# Plain `.env` applies to every project and is unambiguous. Both names are
# gitignored (root `.gitignore` lines 39-40, and `cloud/.gitignore:66`);
# confirm with `git check-ignore -v <path>` before writing either.
#
# ⚠️ AND USE `npx -y firebase-tools@<version>` TO DEPLOY, not the `firebase`
# on your PATH if it is the standalone binary. That build bundles its own
# node 20 + npm 8, and its npm dies in the predeploy hook with
# `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'stdin')` — while the same
# `npm run lint` exits 0 when you run it yourself. CI installs firebase-tools
# through npm for this reason (`.github/workflows/emulator-guards.yml`).
#
# ⚠️ WHY THIS FILE EXISTS AT ALL (AGL-1617).
#
# firebase-functions v2 reads these from a dotenv file in THIS directory at
# deploy time and writes them onto the deployed service. A variable that is not
# here is not set on the function — and on 2026-08-24 that was not theoretical:
# `pluginJobsBeat` was live on revision 00001 from 2026-08-03, with no
# AGLYN_JOB_RUNNER_URL set, still running the pre-AGL-2176 code that carried a
# hardcoded default host. It worked only because that default happens to be a
# host on Aglyn's own deployment.
#
# So a full `firebase deploy --only functions` from a checkout with no dotenv
# file would have deployed the current source — which correctly has NO default
# — with the variable still unset, and stopped scheduled publishing and
# booking-hold expiry platform-wide, silently, with the only symptom a
# `plugin-jobs-beat: job-silent` row on /api/health/crons half an hour later.
#
# Secrets do NOT go here. `PLUGIN_JOBS_SECRET` and `CRON_SECRET` are bound from
# Secret Manager (`firebase functions:secrets:set <NAME>`); this file is for
# configuration that is not a credential.

# Tenant origin `pluginJobsBeat` POSTs every minute — scheduled publishing and
# booking-hold expiry. Any host on YOUR deployment works; it must be one of
# yours (AGL-2176). No default: unset, the beat refuses to fire and logs why.
AGLYN_JOB_RUNNER_URL=https://sites.example.com/api/plugins/run-jobs

# Origin that SERVES your console. `consoleFastCrons` POSTs it every fifteen
# minutes for scheduled campaign sends and pending custom-domain completion
# (AGL-1617). Not a host that REDIRECTS to the console — a redirect drops the
# POST body and the x-cron-secret header (AGL-786). No default, same reason as
# above.
AGLYN_CONSOLE_URL=https://app.example.com

# OPTIONAL. Vercel Bot Protection bypass, the same token every other
# Aglyn-owned caller of our own hosts sends as `x-aglyn-probe`
# (tools/scripts/lib/probe-headers.mjs). Absent means the header is simply not
# sent, which is right for a console with no bot protection in front of it; on
# a host that has it, an unrecognised automated client gets a 429 checkpoint
# page instead of running the cron.
AGLYN_PROBE_TOKEN=
